  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/87BE39">Definition <span data-tag="87BE39">1.1.5.5</span>.</a>simplicial nervenerve!of a simplicial categoryNervecalC@$\Nerve (\calC )$ Let $\calC $ be a simplicial category. The <em>simplicial nerve</em> $\Nerve (\calC )$ is the simplicial set described by the formula </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \Hom _{ \sSet }( \Delta ^ n, \Nerve (\calC )) = \Hom _{\sCat }( \sCoNerve [ \Delta ^ n ], \calC ). \]
</div>
  <p>If $\calC $ is a topological category, we define the <em>topological</em> <em>nerve</em> $\tNerve (\calC )$ of $\calC $ to be the simplicial nerve of $\Sing \calC $.topological nervenerve!of a topological category </p>
